# Lane ownership: AUTHORITATIVE (PLAN.md §3 links here; content is Migrate's, per D-0198/D-0199/D-0200/D-0219/D-0227/D-0229).
# path-glob<TAB>owner[,owner]  first match wins; '*' crosses '/'; owner '*' = shared (Arch review decides); '#' starts a comment.
# =<token><TAB><bot>: branch bot/<token>[-topic] acts as <bot>. Crossing a lane needs the owner's agreement and a
# 'Cross-Lane: <owner>' trailer (land.sh, reading main's copy); at commit time LWC_CROSS_LANE=<owner> (pre-commit).
# Consumers (shim-gate, lane-check): skip comment lines and =token alias lines by explicit rule; every other
# non-empty line must have ≥2 tab-separated columns (else fail closed).
